From def7de15f33d80e7e280f322c83194267df6b075 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:34:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ai): stop the endless 'timed out after 45s' in the Pebby
 chat

Pebby ships the whole database knowledge snapshot (~40k tokens) to the
provider on every question, so slow-but-healthy OpenAI-compatible
endpoints routinely blew through the hard 45s per-call abort and every
message failed with the same generic timeout error.

- raise the per-call provider timeout 45s -> 90s
- add a 110s whole-request budget; the web-research round now runs only
  with the time that is left (and is skipped gracefully instead of
  double-timing-out the question)
- export maxDuration = 120 for the route so Vercel keeps the function
  alive for the full budget instead of killing it at the plan default
- classify provider failures into actionable messages (DNS failure,
  connection refused, interrupted, timeout) naming the provider host,
  on both runtimes (Node/undici on Vercel and Bun self-hosted)
- chat widget + settings Test button: parse the /api/ai response
  defensively so a platform 504 HTML page no longer crashes with
  'Unexpected token <'
- chat widget: live elapsed-seconds counter and a 'provider is slow'
  hint after 30s so long waits no longer look frozen

Verified live: refused/DNS/timeout(90s)/provider-HTTP paths all return
the intended messages; eslint + tsc clean; production build passes.
